
 Agenda

1. Competition Requirements & Objectives (10-20 min)
- Review relevant competition rules, deliverables, and constraints.
- Identify the problems the electronics system must solve.
- Discuss interfaces with other rocket subsystems.
2. Problem Definition & System Requirements (10-20 min)
- Identify key functions, operational needs, and potential failure modes.
- Draft initial system-level requirements (i.e., system shall record flight data at a defined sample rate).
- Establish priorities and identify open questions.
3. Component Requirements & Specifications (15-25 min) - (tentative on this, might want to spend more time on problem definitions and system-level thinking for first electronics focus meeting)
- Break system requirements into component-level needs.
- Identify preliminary performance, electrical, mechanical, environmental, and interface specifications.
- Distinguish required capabilities from potential implementation solutions.
4. Action Items & Follow-Up Planning (5-10 min)
- Assign owners for investigating requirements and unresolved questions.
- Identify information needed before selecting components or architectures.
- Establish deliverables and priorities for the next meeting(s) this week.
